          "stable_key": "os.processes_threads",
          "title": "Processes & Threads",
          "est_effort_min": 60,
          "priority": 4,
          "depends_on": [],
          "diagnostic_probe": "What's the key difference between a process and a thread in terms of memory sharing?",
          "diagnostic_answer": "Each process has its own isolated address space. Threads within the same process share that address space (heap, globals) but each has its own stack and registers — so threads are cheaper to create/switch but must coordinate access to shared memory."
