          "est_effort_min": 60,
          "priority": 5,
          "depends_on": ["dbms.sql.basics"],
          "diagnostic_probe": "What does the 'I' in ACID guarantee, and what problem does it prevent?",
          "diagnostic_answer": "'I' is Isolation — concurrent transactions produce the same result as if they had run one after another, serially. It prevents problems like dirty reads, where one transaction sees another's uncommitted changes."
